(142851, 7128, 3416, '<td valign="top">Excellent, nonsingle by the effect of the eye, the illumination, the approach, the expression and ancuadre they make of this photography an art work.  10 jcof</td>', 'Excellent, nonsingle by the effect of the eye, the illumination, the approach, the expression and ancuadre they make of this photography an art work.  10 jcof', '2002-10-18 18:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(142852, 7128, 3454, '<td valign="top">Very interested to see how you acheived this shot, great submission.</td>', 'Very interested to see how you acheived this shot, great submission.', '2002-10-18 22:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(142853, 7128, 4395, '<td valign="top">Very very cool! <br/></td>', 'Very very cool! ', '2002-10-19 18:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(142854, 7128, 2221, '<td valign="top">Excellent! Personally I love photo''s of this kind where one colour sticks out. And in this case it''s not just a cheap effect but serves the purpose of the photo. Composition, lighting  and focus (well chosen DOF) are also very good. I guess many will gripe about the "overexposure". It''s not! It adds to the stark expression. I especially like the wrinkles which express the emotion perfectly. This is one of my favourite photos this week. Good job! -stephan</td>', 'Excellent! Personally I love photo''s of this kind where one colour sticks out. And in this case it''s not just a cheap effect but serves the purpose of the photo. Composition, lighting  and focus (well chosen DOF) are also very good. I guess many will gripe about the "overexposure". It''s not! It adds to the stark expression. I especially like the wrinkles which express the emotion perfectly. This is one of my favourite photos this week. Good job! -stephan', '2002-10-20 22:05:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(142855, 7128, 2247, '<td valign="top">Ohhhhh. . . .He looks REALLY angry!  Nicely done.</td>', 'Ohhhhh. . . .He looks REALLY angry!  Nicely done.', '2002-10-20 23:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(142856, 7128, 2923, '<td valign="top">interesting. 7</td>', 'interesting. 7', '2002-10-20 23:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(142857, 7128, 1897, '<td valign="top">I will not believe that this was legally edited until I have learned how, which I have asked for, but did not recieve.  A desaturation would not give this affect.</td>', 'I will not believe that this was legally edited until I have learned how, which I have asked for, but did not recieve.  A desaturation would not give this affect.', '2002-10-21 02:22:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(142858, 7128, 843, '<td valign="top">First of all, I e-mailed you a description of my steps during the voting, and desaturation was only TWO STEPS out of SIX or SEVEN. I''ll post my original tomorrow for all to look at, but for now here are the basic steps (which you DID recieve):<br/><br/>(first of all I was wearing blue contacts)<br/>Curves (blue channel, to boost the eye color)<br/>Desaturate all colors but blue<br/>Change blue hue to red, adjusting saturation &amp; lightness also<br/>Desaturate all colors but red, boost red saturation<br/>Curve adjustments, unsharp mask, etc. (nothing to do with the eye)</td>', 'First of all, I e-mailed you a description of my steps during the voting, and desaturation was only TWO STEPS out of SIX or SEVEN. I''ll post my original tomorrow for all to look at, but for now here are the basic steps (which you DID recieve):(first of all I was wearing blue contacts)Curves (blue channel, to boost the eye color)Desaturate all colors but blueChange blue hue to red, adjusting saturation & lightness alsoDesaturate all colors but red, boost red saturationCurve adjustments, unsharp mask, etc. (nothing to do with the eye)', '2002-10-21 02:47:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(142859, 7128, 2923, '<td valign="top">Isn''t desaturation and adjust BLUE channel in violation of spot editing?  I mean, you are only changing one aspect of the color spectrum, not the whole image as with RGB curves adjustment (to all colors)....  just wondering how the rules are supposed to work :)</td>', 'Isn''t desaturation and adjust BLUE channel in violation of spot editing?  I mean, you are only changing one aspect of the color spectrum, not the whole image as with RGB curves adjustment (to all colors)....  just wondering how the rules are supposed to work :)', '2002-10-21 03:41:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(142860, 7128, 843, '<td valign="top">It is changing the whole image...all blue in the image.</td>', 'It is changing the whole image...all blue in the image.', '2002-10-21 03:45:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(142861, 7128, 255, '<td valign="top">nice finish greenem! i love this.</td>', 'nice finish greenem! i love this.', '2002-10-21 04:41:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(142862, 7128, 1897, '<td valign="top">There is nothing wrong with Desat. or adjusting one channel, that is just like adjusting the color, but I do not understand the uneven outline around the eye, or how it looks layers.  A step-by-step, how''d they do that would be quite insightful I think.</td>', 'There is nothing wrong with Desat. or adjusting one channel, that is just like adjusting the color, but I do not understand the uneven outline around the eye, or how it looks layers.  A step-by-step, how''d they do that would be quite insightful I think.', '2002-10-21 12:19:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(142863, 7128, 1897, '<td valign="top">I should say "sorry" for wording the first post rudely, and you did reply to my comment on your photo the first time.<br/><br/>If this were really done legally, you do know some tricks.  I still am bothered by sharp line around the red in the eye.</td>', 'I should say "sorry" for wording the first post rudely, and you did reply to my comment on your photo the first time.If this were really done legally, you do know some tricks.  I still am bothered by sharp line around the red in the eye.', '2002-10-21 14:37:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(142864, 7128, 205, '<td valign="top">Can you do this with out photoshop?</td>', 'Can you do this with out photoshop?', '2002-10-21 14:43:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(142865, 7128, 1054, '<td valign="top">Anarchos, the equivalent functionality exists in the Gimp.  Zeissman, color contacts would create this sharp outline as they would not match the color of the rest of the eye.  Greenem2, impressive work!</td>', 'Anarchos, the equivalent functionality exists in the Gimp.  Zeissman, color contacts would create this sharp outline as they would not match the color of the rest of the eye.  Greenem2, impressive work!', '2002-10-21 15:40:00.000000', NULL, 0),
