(192351, 6979, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrJOnes:</b></div><hr/><i>Brilliantly lighted. Very well done composition. Excellent framing. Right on par with the theme...</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Maybe a little too-brilliantly lighted...I think I''m expecting it to look dimmer and softer, as if from candles or lamplight. You''d risk lose some detail, but might add to the mood.<br/>You might try using a tone curve on adjustment layer to add a yellowish cast without losing the contrast and detail.</td>', 'Originally posted by DrJOnes:Brilliantly lighted. Very well done composition. Excellent framing. Right on par with the theme... Maybe a little too-brilliantly lighted...I think I''m expecting it to look dimmer and softer, as if from candles or lamplight. You''d risk lose some detail, but might add to the mood.You might try using a tone curve on adjustment layer to add a yellowish cast without losing the contrast and detail.', '2003-01-15 22:11:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(192353, 6979, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by shawna:</b></div><hr/><i>The syringe should have a needle if it''s too be effective. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Some people use a syringe <i>sans</i> needle to administer drugs intra-nasally. I don''t think it''s very comfortable, but it does lower the risk of contracting AIDS, syphilis, hepatitis, endocarditis, or necrotizing fasciitis.</td>', 'Originally posted by shawna:The syringe should have a needle if it''s too be effective.  Some people use a syringe sans needle to administer drugs intra-nasally. I don''t think it''s very comfortable, but it does lower the risk of contracting AIDS, syphilis, hepatitis, endocarditis, or necrotizing fasciitis.', '2003-01-15 22:19:51.000000', NULL, 0),
